# CAP-9C1 trusted build-time QuickJS plugin list.
#
# BUILD-TIME ONLY. This file is never shipped, never read at runtime and
# never reachable from script. It names which already-written plugin
# source trees the private packaging tool turns into plugins.zip plus a
# generated native registry, and nothing else:
#
#   - it carries NO capability. Capabilities come from the CAP-8 policy
#     keyed by PrincipalId, so the packaging path cannot grant a right;
#   - it carries NO resource bound. The generator emits the ratified
#     defaults, so a tampered copy of this file cannot raise a memory
#     cap or switch a CPU bound off;
#   - it cannot register a plugin at runtime. The runtime trusts only
#     the COMPILED registry generated from it.
#
# Grammar: the repository's `key = value` lock-file shape. '#' starts a
# comment, blank lines are ignored, ASCII only, no escape sequences, and
# each `plugin` line opens a block that must carry exactly one
# principal, one root and one entry. The eight security-authority key
# names are refused loudly rather than ignored.
#
# The manifest "id" inside each root must equal its plugin id: the
# archive sub-tree, the native PluginId and the descriptive manifest id
# are ONE name.

plugin    = quickjs.calculator
principal = plugin:calculator
root      = examples/07-quickjs/plugins/quickjs.calculator
entry     = main.js

plugin    = quickjs.reporting
principal = plugin:reporting
root      = examples/07-quickjs/plugins/quickjs.reporting
entry     = main.js
